Single solitary wave initialized with DJL equation using DJLES 1.11 in matlab set up for bounday layer test

The wave is initialized in the mfile mfiles/write_initial_DJL.m
which reads in the grid from suntans output and creates input files for the
velocity field (the dot product of u with the normal), density (salinity), and free surface based on a desired wave APE. The generation will work for sigma, hybrid, or isopycnal coordinates. 

Set vertcoord = 2 for sigma/z-level (since it is a rigid lid) and vertcoord = 4 for iso/hybrid. Hybrid layer counts are set in suntans.dat as well. 
The midlayers set in suntans.dat is used in the suntans update step. However, a different midlayers value likely needs to be set in the matlab initialization code 
in order to generate that many midlayers after removing large isopycnals, etc. This value is set in the mfile directly. It is generally 1-2 less than the listed 
suntans midlayers value and can be checked by checking the stretching of the mid layers. 

Be sure to set advectSalinity and advectTemp to 0 for isopycnals and 1 otherwise.

For QUICK, set any TVD variable in suntans.dat to 5. For SHARP, set to 6.

"Make test" will run the script BL_test.sh.

Nx, sh_val, and Atarget are all set directly in the script and are currently set to reasonable values. sh_val is 10x the fractional height of the pycnolcine (ie sh_val=2 will have the pycnocline at -0.2*H) and Atarget is the target APE for the DJL solver, which will lead to a certain amplitude. 

rundata/suntans.dat includes model parameters. To test different momentum advection schemes:
    - For original SUNTANS central-differencing: set nonlinear=2
    - For new conservative momentums scheme: set nonlinear=0 and TVDmom to scheme of choice
        - In current version, TVDmom=3 is Superbee, TVDmom=4 is vanLeer, and TVDmom=5 is central-differencing

grid paramaters (domain size, horizontal resolution) are set in mfiles/quadgridperiodic.m. If a different grid generator is used, comment out the line in the script that runs quadgridperiodic.m, place the generated grid files in rundata/ and proceed. 

To run, type: 
    make test
  
Which compiles the example directory and runs the BL_test.sh script

Current grid is 10x or so less resolved than it should be to allow for quick testing. 

Requires parallel toolbox in Matlab for init.